## The Asset Bible

Your **Asset Bible** is the foundation of your production. By defining characters upfront, you ensure that StoryBook's
AI generates consistent visuals and voices across every episode.

## Creating a New Character

1. Navigate to **Assets → Characters**.
2. Click **New Character**.

### Key Fields

- **Name**: The character's full name.
- **Description**: A physical description used for image generation. Be specific about age, hair, clothes, and
distinctive features.
> *Example: "A gruff detective in his 50s, wearing a beige trench coat, stubble, scar on left cheek."*
- **Personality**: Defines how the AI writes their dialogue (e.g., "Sarcastic, impatient, uses slang").
- **Voice**: Assign a voice profile for text-to-speech generation.

### Reference Images

Upload a high-quality portrait of your character. This serves as the "Face ID" for video generation models, helping them
keep the character recognizable in different scenes.

## Editing & deleting

Detailed character profiles lead to better storytelling. You can edit a character at any time to refine their
description or update their reference image.

> [!TIP]
> Changes to a character will only apply to *newly generated* content. Existing shots or scenes won't be automatically
updated.